div.p:
This study should examine policy towards COCOM, U.S. differential controls, trade
                    with Eastern Europe, Asian communist and Cuban trade embargos, and
                    extraterritorial effects of trade controls, by treating the following elements: 

—the effectiveness of present measures;

—the strategic impact of these controls upon communist
                            countries;

—relations with our allies;

—other relevant factors including U.S. exports, our balance of
                            payments and relations between the U.S. Government, on the one hand, and
                            U.S. business and labor, on the other.
